   "kg_test": "test/test_lisp.c (not yet written -- Phase 8 Wave D delivers defcustom and its test together)",
   "rationale": "Phase 8 Wave D (parent plan's init-compat-waves phase, milestone 2): owned by kg, prelude/library layer, comparison emacs. Delivered as a prelude macro over kg's existing defvar-shaped boundp/setq machinery, not a port of Custom. Its eventual cases must distinguish: an unbound variable from an already-bound one (same first-defvar-wins contract as defvar); whether the standard-value form is evaluated in each of those two cases; the returned symbol and the stored docstring; accepted, inert presentation metadata (:type, :options, :group, :tag, :link, :version, :package-version) that kg stores but never interprets; rejected semantics-bearing or unknown keywords (kg is not silently accepting an arbitrary keyword and pretending it did something); and the documented absence of dynamic binding, retained standard forms, setopt, and any Customize UI. This entry exists specifically so defcustom does not become either a hand-waved synonym for defvar or an accidental commitment to all of Custom.",
